MODULE: auth
FILES: src/lib/auth.ts, src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts, middleware.ts, src/app/providers.tsx
RESPONSIBILITY: NextAuth.js v4 authentication with Credentials provider, JWT sessions, route protection
KEY_FILES:
- src/lib/auth.ts: NextAuth config with Credentials provider, bcrypt verification, JWT callbacks, ~65 lines
- src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts: NextAuth API route handler (GET/POST), ~6 lines
- middleware.ts: getToken-based middleware protecting /admin/* routes, redirects to /admin/login, ~30 lines
- src/app/providers.tsx: SessionProvider wrapper for client components, ~7 lines
DEPENDENCIES:
- uses: next-auth@^4.24.14: authentication framework (v4, not Auth.js v5)
- uses: bcrypt@^6.0.0: password hashing and comparison
- imports: @/lib/prisma: prisma client for AdminUser queries
- imports: next-auth/jwt: getToken for middleware token verification
INTERFACES:
- authOptions: NextAuthOptions object exported from src/lib/auth.ts
- middleware: default export from middleware.ts, matcher ["/admin/:path*"]
- Providers: SessionProvider wrapper component from src/app/providers.tsx
TRAPS:
- [HIGH] Login page must NOT be wrapped by admin layout — use route group (admin) for layout/dashboard, keep login outside | FIX: src/app/admin/(admin)/layout.tsx wraps only authenticated pages
- [HIGH] Next.js App Router route groups with parentheses: (admin) directory does NOT add to URL path | FIX: /admin/(admin)/dashboard/page.tsx resolves to /admin/dashboard
- [LOW] NextAuth v4 uses next-auth/react for client (signIn, signOut, useSession) and next-auth for server (NextAuth, getServerSession) | FIX: don't mix v4 and v5 API patterns
- [LOW] middleware.ts uses getToken from next-auth/jwt, not withAuth — lighter weight, more control | FIX: check token manually, redirect with NextResponse.redirect
CHANGELOG:
- F-002 | add: NextAuth.js v4 with Credentials provider and JWT sessions
- F-002 | add: middleware for /admin/* route protection
- F-002 | add: SessionProvider wrapper in root layout
